  "title": "Oil struck at Masjed Soleyman, Persia",
  "summary": "On 26 May 1908, at about 4 a.m., drillers led by the engineer George Bernard Reynolds struck oil at 1,180 feet in Well No. 1 at Masjed Soleyman in south-west Persia. The well, drilled for William Knox D'Arcy's concession, flowed as a gusher more than 80 feet high.",
